    "methods_description": "Data were collected using 8 Brain Vision Amplifiers with 120 EEG scalp electrodes, 110 noise electrodes, and 8 EMG electrodes (sternocleidomastoid and trapezius). Loadsol insoles recorded ground reaction forces and an APDM Opal IMU was placed on the lower back. Participants wore liquid crystal goggles generating intermittent visual occlusions while walking on a treadmill at 0.0, 0.4, 0.8, 1.2, and 1.6 m/s for 3-minute trials, with occlusion events occurring every 8-10 seconds lasting 1.5 seconds. Walking speed order was randomized across participants.",
